 "result": "All in `src/tessel/views.py`:\n\n- **`View.to_view_func(cls, *class_args, **class_kwargs)`** (line 86) builds the view function. The inner `view(**kwargs)` (lines 106/115) instantiates `view.view_class` on every request, then calls `self.run_view(**kwargs)` (sync-wrapped via `ensure_sync`). It also sets `view.view_class = cls` and `view.methods = cls.methods`, so route registration knows the allowed HTTP methods.\n- **`VerbView.__init_subclass__`** (line 165) auto-populates `cls.methods` by merging base-class methods with any `get`/`post`/etc. defined on the class (checked against `http_method_funcs`, upper-cased).\n- **`VerbView.run_view`** (line 182) does the dispatch: `getattr(self, request.method.lower())`, falling back to `get` for HEAD when there's no handler. It asserts the handler exists and calls it with the URL kwargs.\n\nRouting is done by registering `Class.to_view_func(\"name\")` with `app.attach_route_rule(...)` (see the docstring example around line 160).",
